      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"The Travelling Botanist problem\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "image: 'botanicmap.png'\n",
        "categories: [Combinatorics, Algorithms, Discrete maths, Optimisation]\n",
        "filters:\n",
        "  - shinylive\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "Imagine an exhibition trail around the Botanic Gardens, with a fixed set of stops -- numbered markers a visitor could walk round. If you wanted to visit every stop and come back to where you started, covering as little ground as possible, which order should you go in?\n",
        "\n",
        "This is the **Travelling Salesman Problem** (TSP) -- one of the most famous problems in the whole of mathematics and computer science. It sounds almost too simple to be interesting: just try every possible order of stops and keep the shortest one. The catch is *how many* orders there are. With 5 stops there are only 12 distinct routes to check. With 10 stops there are already 181,440. With 20 stops there are over 60 quadrillion -- so many that a computer checking a billion routes every single second would still need about two years to get through them all. Trying every option, which works fine for a handful of stops, becomes hopeless almost immediately -- and no computer, however fast, escapes that by brute force alone.\n",
        "\n",
        "That collision -- a problem you can *state* to a ten-year-old, that *defeats* every computer on Earth once it gets big enough -- is exactly why mathematicians and computer scientists still work on it. Real versions of this problem sit behind delivery route planning, circuit board drilling, and DNA sequencing.\n",
        "\n",
        "The map below shows five real stops from our Botanic Gardens exhibition trail: **1. The Glass House Cactus Garden**, **2. The Chalet**, **3. The Good Grief Garden**, **4. The Patterson Education Centre**, and **5. The Eddie Kemp Pavilion**.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Click stops to select them** -- choose a handful (at least 3) to build a route around.\n",
        "- Switch to **\"Adds the next stop to your route\"** and click your selected stops in whatever order you think gives the shortest trip. That's your manually-built route.\n",
        "- Compare it against a fast **algorithm route** (nearest neighbour, optionally cleaned up with a technique called 2-opt), and, since there are only 5 stops here, the **exact optimal route** found by checking every possibility.\n",
        "- Use the toggle to switch which route is drawn on the map, and watch how close your own guess gets to optimal.\n",
        "\n",
        "If you're visiting the exhibition in person, look out for a QR code at each stop. Scanning it opens this page and automatically checks that stop in on your phone -- your visited stops build up under **\"Your physical visit\"** in the sidebar, in the order you actually walked them, and once you've found all five the app shows you how your real walking route compares to the mathematically optimal one.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {#fig-tsp}\n",
        "```{shinylive-python}\n",
        "#| standalone: true\n",
        "#| components: [viewer]\n",
        "#| viewerHeight: 700\n",
        "\n",
        "## file: app.py\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import math\n",
        "import itertools\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "from shiny import App, Inputs, Outputs, Session, render, ui, reactive\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import matplotlib.image as mpimg\n",
        "\n",
        "appdir = Path(__file__).parent\n",
        "IMG_PATH = appdir / \"botanicmap.png\"\n",
        "img = mpimg.imread(str(IMG_PATH))\n",
        "H, W = img.shape[0], img.shape[1]\n",
        "\n",
        "BRUTE_FORCE_LIMIT = 9\n",
        "CLICK_TOLERANCE = 0.035 * W\n",
        "QR_STORAGE_KEY = \"tsp_qr_visits_v1\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fixed exhibition stops -- pixel coordinates on botanicmap.png.\n",
        "# Stop 1 is STOPS[0] / STOP_NAMES[0], matching the \"stop=1\" QR code, and so on.\n",
        "STOPS = [\n",
        "    (96, 108),   # 1. The Glass House Cactus Garden\n",
        "    (219, 77),   # 2. The Chalet\n",
        "    (272, 69),   # 3. The Good Grief Garden\n",
        "    (224, 133),  # 4. The Patterson Education Centre\n",
        "    (298, 174),  # 5. The Eddie Kemp Pavilion\n",
        "]\n",
        "STOP_NAMES = [\n",
        "    \"The Glass House Cactus Garden\",\n",
        "    \"The Chalet\",\n",
        "    \"The Good Grief Garden\",\n",
        "    \"The Patterson Education Centre\",\n",
        "    \"The Eddie Kemp Pavilion\",\n",
        "]\n",
        "N_STOPS = len(STOPS)\n",
        "\n",
        "QR_JS = f\"\"\"\n",
        "$(document).on('shiny:connected', function(event) {{\n",
        "  // Shiny's own client sends its \"init\" message synchronously right after\n",
        "  // triggering this event (see shiny.js socket.onopen). If we call\n",
        "  // Shiny.setInputValue() immediately here, our \"update\" message can reach\n",
        "  // the server BEFORE that \"init\" message, which the server rejects with\n",
        "  // ProtocolError: Invalid method for the current session state. Deferring\n",
        "  // with setTimeout(..., 0) pushes our call to the next tick, after Shiny's\n",
        "  // own init message (and any pending messages) have already been sent.\n",
        "  setTimeout(function() {{\n",
        "    try {{\n",
        "      var params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);\n",
        "      var stopParam = params.get('stop');\n",
        "      var key = '{QR_STORAGE_KEY}';\n",
        "      var stored = localStorage.getItem(key);\n",
        "      var visits = stored ? JSON.parse(stored) : [];\n",
        "\n",
        "      if (stopParam !== null) {{\n",
        "        var stopNum = parseInt(stopParam, 10);\n",
        "        if (!isNaN(stopNum)) {{\n",
        "          var already = visits.some(function(v) {{ return v.stop === stopNum; }});\n",
        "          if (!already) {{\n",
        "            visits.push({{stop: stopNum, ts: new Date().toISOString()}});\n",
        "            localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(visits));\n",
        "          }}\n",
        "        }}\n",
        "      }}\n",
        "      Shiny.setInputValue('qr_visits', JSON.stringify(visits), {{priority: 'event'}});\n",
        "    }} catch (e) {{\n",
        "      console.error('QR check-in error:', e);\n",
        "      Shiny.setInputValue('qr_visits', '[]', {{priority: 'event'}});\n",
        "    }}\n",
        "  }}, 0);\n",
        "}});\n",
        "\n",
        "Shiny.addCustomMessageHandler('clear_qr_visits', function(message) {{\n",
        "  try {{\n",
        "    localStorage.removeItem('{QR_STORAGE_KEY}');\n",
        "  }} catch (e) {{\n",
        "    console.error('clear error', e);\n",
        "  }}\n",
        "  // Navigate to the bare page path rather than location.reload(): if the\n",
        "  // current URL still has a \"?stop=N\" query string (e.g. the visitor just\n",
        "  // scanned the last QR code and then tapped this button), a plain reload\n",
        "  // would immediately re-add that stop from the URL, undoing the clear.\n",
        "  window.location.href = window.location.pathname;\n",
        "}});\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def route_length(order, stops):\n",
        "    total = 0.0\n",
        "    n = len(order)\n",
        "    for i in range(n):\n",
        "        ax_, ay_ = stops[order[i]]\n",
        "        bx_, by_ = stops[order[(i + 1) % n]]\n",
        "        total += math.hypot(ax_ - bx_, ay_ - by_)\n",
        "    return total\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def open_path_length(order, stops):\n",
        "    total = 0.0\n",
        "    for i in range(len(order) - 1):\n",
        "        ax_, ay_ = stops[order[i]]\n",
        "        bx_, by_ = stops[order[i + 1]]\n",
        "        total += math.hypot(ax_ - bx_, ay_ - by_)\n",
        "    return total\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def nearest_neighbour(indices, stops):\n",
        "    remaining = set(indices[1:])\n",
        "    order = [indices[0]]\n",
        "    while remaining:\n",
        "        last = order[-1]\n",
        "        lx, ly = stops[last]\n",
        "        nxt = min(remaining, key=lambda j: math.hypot(lx - stops[j][0], ly - stops[j][1]))\n",
        "        order.append(nxt)\n",
        "        remaining.remove(nxt)\n",
        "    return order\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def two_opt(order, stops):\n",
        "    order = order[:]\n",
        "    n = len(order)\n",
        "    improved = True\n",
        "    while improved:\n",
        "        improved = False\n",
        "        for i in range(n - 1):\n",
        "            for j in range(i + 2, n):\n",
        "                if i == 0 and j == n - 1:\n",
        "                    continue\n",
        "                a, b = order[i], order[i + 1]\n",
        "                c, d = order[j], order[(j + 1) % n]\n",
        "                old = math.hypot(stops[a][0] - stops[b][0], stops[a][1] - stops[b][1]) + math.hypot(\n",
        "                    stops[c][0] - stops[d][0], stops[c][1] - stops[d][1]\n",
        "                )\n",
        "                new = math.hypot(stops[a][0] - stops[c][0], stops[a][1] - stops[c][1]) + math.hypot(\n",
        "                    stops[b][0] - stops[d][0], stops[b][1] - stops[d][1]\n",
        "                )\n",
        "                if new < old - 1e-9:\n",
        "                    order[i + 1 : j + 1] = reversed(order[i + 1 : j + 1])\n",
        "                    improved = True\n",
        "    return order\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def brute_force(indices, stops):\n",
        "    best_order = None\n",
        "    best_len = math.inf\n",
        "    first = indices[0]\n",
        "    rest = indices[1:]\n",
        "    for perm in itertools.permutations(rest):\n",
        "        order = [first] + list(perm)\n",
        "        length = route_length(order, stops)\n",
        "        if length < best_len:\n",
        "            best_len = length\n",
        "            best_order = order\n",
        "    return best_order, best_len\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def nearest_stop(cx, cy):\n",
        "    best_i, best_d = None, CLICK_TOLERANCE\n",
        "    for i, (x, y) in enumerate(STOPS):\n",
        "        d = math.hypot(x - cx, y - cy)\n",
        "        if d < best_d:\n",
        "            best_i, best_d = i, d\n",
        "    return best_i\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "stop_legend = \", \".join(f\"{i + 1} = {name}\" for i, name in enumerate(STOP_NAMES))\n",
        "\n",
        "app_ui = ui.page_sidebar(\n",
        "    ui.sidebar(\n",
        "        ui.h5(\"Simulate a route\"),\n",
        "        ui.markdown(f\"_{stop_legend}_\"),\n",
        "        ui.input_radio_buttons(\n",
        "            \"click_mode\",\n",
        "            \"Clicking the map:\",\n",
        "            {\"select\": \"Selects / deselects stops\", \"route\": \"Adds the next stop to your route\"},\n",
        "            selected=\"select\",\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        ui.row(\n",
        "            ui.column(6, ui.input_action_button(\"clear_selection\", \"Clear stops\", width=\"100%\")),\n",
        "            ui.column(6, ui.input_action_button(\"clear_route\", \"Clear my route\", width=\"100%\")),\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        ui.hr(),\n",
        "        ui.input_radio_buttons(\n",
        "            \"method\",\n",
        "            \"Algorithm route\",\n",
        "            {\"nn\": \"Nearest neighbour\", \"nn2opt\": \"Nearest neighbour + 2-opt\"},\n",
        "            selected=\"nn2opt\",\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        ui.input_checkbox(\n",
        "            \"exact\",\n",
        "            \"Also find the exact best route (feasible up to about 9 stops)\",\n",
        "            value=False,\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        ui.hr(),\n",
        "        ui.input_radio_buttons(\n",
        "            \"show\",\n",
        "            \"Show on the map\",\n",
        "            {\n",
        "                \"manual\": \"Your simulated route\",\n",
        "                \"algo\": \"Algorithm route\",\n",
        "                \"exact\": \"Optimal route\",\n",
        "                \"qr\": \"Your QR check-ins (physical visit)\",\n",
        "            },\n",
        "            selected=\"algo\",\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        ui.hr(),\n",
        "        ui.output_text_verbatim(\"summary\"),\n",
        "        ui.hr(),\n",
        "        ui.h5(\"Your physical visit\"),\n",
        "        ui.markdown(\"_Scan the QR code at a stop to check in -- this device remembers your visits._\"),\n",
        "        ui.output_ui(\"qr_status\"),\n",
        "        ui.input_action_button(\"clear_qr\", \"Clear my visit (this device)\", width=\"100%\"),\n",
        "        width=360,\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    ui.output_plot(\"plot\", click=True),\n",
        "    ui.tags.script(QR_JS),\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def server(input: Inputs, output: Outputs, session: Session):\n",
        "    selected = reactive.Value(set())\n",
        "    manual_route = reactive.Value([])\n",
        "\n",
        "    @reactive.Effect\n",
        "    @reactive.event(input.clear_selection)\n",
        "    def _():\n",
        "        selected.set(set())\n",
        "        manual_route.set([])\n",
        "\n",
        "    @reactive.Effect\n",
        "    @reactive.event(input.clear_route)\n",
        "    def _():\n",
        "        manual_route.set([])\n",
        "\n",
        "    @reactive.Effect\n",
        "    @reactive.event(input.clear_qr)\n",
        "    async def _():\n",
        "        await session.send_custom_message(\"clear_qr_visits\", {})\n",
        "\n",
        "    @reactive.Effect\n",
        "    @reactive.event(input.plot_click)\n",
        "    def _():\n",
        "        click = input.plot_click()\n",
        "        if click is None:\n",
        "            return\n",
        "        idx = nearest_stop(click[\"x\"], click[\"y\"])\n",
        "        if idx is None:\n",
        "            return\n",
        "\n",
        "        if input.click_mode() == \"select\":\n",
        "            sel = set(selected.get())\n",
        "            if idx in sel:\n",
        "                sel.discard(idx)\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                sel.add(idx)\n",
        "            selected.set(sel)\n",
        "            manual_route.set([])  # selection changed -> your route no longer applies\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            sel = selected.get()\n",
        "            if idx not in sel:\n",
        "                return  # can only route through selected stops\n",
        "            route = manual_route.get()\n",
        "            if idx in route:\n",
        "                return  # each stop used once; use \"Clear my route\" to start over\n",
        "            manual_route.set(route + [idx])\n",
        "\n",
        "    @reactive.Calc\n",
        "    def algo_info():\n",
        "        indices = sorted(selected.get())\n",
        "        n = len(indices)\n",
        "        if n < 3:\n",
        "            return {\"n\": n, \"order\": None, \"length\": None, \"possible\": None, \"exact\": None}\n",
        "\n",
        "        if input.method() == \"nn\":\n",
        "            order = nearest_neighbour(indices, STOPS)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            order = two_opt(nearest_neighbour(indices, STOPS), STOPS)\n",
        "        length = route_length(order, STOPS)\n",
        "        possible = math.factorial(n - 1) // 2  # distinct tours, fixed start, direction symmetry removed\n",
        "\n",
        "        exact = None\n",
        "        if input.exact() and 3 <= n <= BRUTE_FORCE_LIMIT:\n",
        "            best_order, best_len = brute_force(indices, STOPS)\n",
        "            exact = {\"order\": best_order, \"length\": best_len}\n",
        "\n",
        "        return {\"n\": n, \"order\": order, \"length\": length, \"possible\": possible, \"exact\": exact}\n",
        "\n",
        "    @reactive.Calc\n",
        "    def manual_info():\n",
        "        sel = selected.get()\n",
        "        route = manual_route.get()\n",
        "        complete = len(sel) >= 3 and set(route) == sel\n",
        "        length = route_length(route, STOPS) if complete else None\n",
        "        return {\"route\": route, \"complete\": complete, \"length\": length}\n",
        "\n",
        "    @reactive.Calc\n",
        "    def qr_route():\n",
        "        raw = input.qr_visits()\n",
        "        if not raw:\n",
        "            return []\n",
        "        try:\n",
        "            visits = json.loads(raw)\n",
        "        except (json.JSONDecodeError, TypeError):\n",
        "            return []\n",
        "        order = []\n",
        "        for v in visits:\n",
        "            try:\n",
        "                idx = int(v[\"stop\"]) - 1  # QR codes use 1-indexed stop numbers\n",
        "            except (KeyError, ValueError, TypeError):\n",
        "                continue\n",
        "            if 0 <= idx < N_STOPS and idx not in order:\n",
        "                order.append(idx)\n",
        "        return order\n",
        "\n",
        "    @reactive.Calc\n",
        "    def full_algo_info():\n",
        "        # The physical trail always covers every fixed stop, so this always\n",
        "        # compares against ALL of STOPS, independent of the simulator's subset.\n",
        "        indices = list(range(N_STOPS))\n",
        "        order = two_opt(nearest_neighbour(indices, STOPS), STOPS)\n",
        "        length = route_length(order, STOPS)\n",
        "        exact = None\n",
        "        if N_STOPS <= BRUTE_FORCE_LIMIT:\n",
        "            best_order, best_len = brute_force(indices, STOPS)\n",
        "            exact = {\"order\": best_order, \"length\": best_len}\n",
        "        return {\"order\": order, \"length\": length, \"exact\": exact}\n",
        "\n",
        "    @output\n",
        "    @render.plot\n",
        "    def plot():\n",
        "        info = algo_info()\n",
        "        m_info = manual_info()\n",
        "        fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 7 * H / W))\n",
        "        ax.imshow(img, extent=[0, W, H, 0])\n",
        "        ax.set_xlim(0, W)\n",
        "        ax.set_ylim(H, 0)\n",
        "        ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        show = input.show()\n",
        "        route_to_draw = None\n",
        "        closed = True\n",
        "        if show == \"manual\":\n",
        "            route_to_draw = m_info[\"route\"]\n",
        "            closed = m_info[\"complete\"]\n",
        "        elif show == \"algo\":\n",
        "            route_to_draw = info[\"order\"]\n",
        "        elif show == \"exact\":\n",
        "            route_to_draw = info[\"exact\"][\"order\"] if info[\"exact\"] else None\n",
        "        elif show == \"qr\":\n",
        "            route_to_draw = qr_route()\n",
        "            closed = len(route_to_draw) == N_STOPS\n",
        "\n",
        "        if route_to_draw and len(route_to_draw) >= 2:\n",
        "            xs = [STOPS[i][0] for i in route_to_draw]\n",
        "            ys = [STOPS[i][1] for i in route_to_draw]\n",
        "            if closed:\n",
        "                xs.append(STOPS[route_to_draw[0]][0])\n",
        "                ys.append(STOPS[route_to_draw[0]][1])\n",
        "            colour = \"#f4a261\" if show == \"qr\" else \"#e63946\"\n",
        "            ax.plot(xs, ys, \"-\", color=colour, linewidth=2.5, zorder=2)\n",
        "\n",
        "        sel = selected.get()\n",
        "        visited_qr = set(qr_route())\n",
        "        for i, (x, y) in enumerate(STOPS):\n",
        "            is_selected = i in sel\n",
        "            is_qr_visited = i in visited_qr\n",
        "            if is_qr_visited:\n",
        "                colour = \"#f4a261\"\n",
        "            elif is_selected:\n",
        "                colour = \"#2a9d8f\"\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                colour = \"#adb5bd\"\n",
        "            ax.scatter(\n",
        "                [x], [y], s=170, color=colour, edgecolor=\"white\", linewidth=1.5,\n",
        "                zorder=3, alpha=1.0 if (is_selected or is_qr_visited) else 0.6,\n",
        "            )\n",
        "            ax.annotate(\n",
        "                str(i + 1), (x, y), color=\"white\", ha=\"center\", va=\"center\",\n",
        "                fontsize=9, fontweight=\"bold\", zorder=4,\n",
        "            )\n",
        "\n",
        "        return fig\n",
        "\n",
        "    @output\n",
        "    @render.text\n",
        "    def summary():\n",
        "        info = algo_info()\n",
        "        m_info = manual_info()\n",
        "        n = info[\"n\"]\n",
        "        lines = [f\"Stops selected: {n} of {N_STOPS}\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "        if n < 3:\n",
        "            lines.append(\"Select at least 3 stops to build a route.\")\n",
        "            return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n",
        "\n",
        "        lines.append(f\"Possible distinct routes: {info['possible']:,}\")\n",
        "        lines.append(\"\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        method_name = \"nearest neighbour\" if input.method() == \"nn\" else \"nearest neighbour + 2-opt\"\n",
        "        lines.append(f\"Algorithm ({method_name}): {info['length']:.0f} units\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        if m_info[\"complete\"]:\n",
        "            lines.append(f\"Your simulated route: {m_info['length']:.0f} units\")\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            lines.append(f\"Your simulated route: {len(m_info['route'])} of {n} stops placed\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        if input.exact():\n",
        "            if info[\"exact\"] is not None:\n",
        "                exact_len = info[\"exact\"][\"length\"]\n",
        "                lines.append(f\"Optimal route: {exact_len:.0f} units\")\n",
        "\n",
        "                algo_pct = 100 * (info[\"length\"] - exact_len) / exact_len if exact_len > 0 else 0\n",
        "                if algo_pct > 0.05:\n",
        "                    lines.append(f\"  algorithm is {algo_pct:.1f}% longer than optimal\")\n",
        "                else:\n",
        "                    lines.append(\"  algorithm found the optimal route!\")\n",
        "\n",
        "                if m_info[\"complete\"]:\n",
        "                    manual_pct = 100 * (m_info[\"length\"] - exact_len) / exact_len if exact_len > 0 else 0\n",
        "                    if manual_pct > 0.05:\n",
        "                        lines.append(f\"  your route is {manual_pct:.1f}% longer than optimal\")\n",
        "                    else:\n",
        "                        lines.append(\"  your route found the optimal route!\")\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                lines.append(\n",
        "                    f\"With {n} stops there are {math.factorial(n):,} possible orderings to check \"\n",
        "                    \"one-by-one -- far too many to try them all.\"\n",
        "                )\n",
        "\n",
        "        return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n",
        "\n",
        "    @output\n",
        "    @render.ui\n",
        "    def qr_status():\n",
        "        route = qr_route()\n",
        "        n = len(route)\n",
        "        if n == 0:\n",
        "            return ui.markdown(\"_No check-ins yet on this device. Scan a QR code at a stop to begin!_\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        names = \", \".join(f\"{i + 1}. {STOP_NAMES[i]}\" for i in route)\n",
        "        last_name = STOP_NAMES[route[-1]]\n",
        "        lines = [f\"**Checked in at {n} of {N_STOPS} stops.** Latest: {last_name}.\"]\n",
        "        lines.append(f\"\\nOrder so far: {names}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        if n >= 2:\n",
